WEBVTT

00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:03.500
Don't worry.

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:06.660
We don't expect you to understand.

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:09.750
I doubt you can.

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:12.030
Not since all you do is steal.

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:15.630
Our creativity is in here.

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:17.180
That's enough.

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:19.240
We don't need false power.

00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:22.830
Since it's come to this...

00:00:23.110 --> 00:00:26.790
I'll do whatever it takes 
to bring you back with us!

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:34.320
What is that?

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:36.730
Is it... a black hole?

00:00:48.110 --> 00:00:51.860
This is a capturing device produced 
by another planet's civilization.

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:57.820
Using this, I'll be able to quickly take your 
creativity back to space in perfect condition.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:01.140
Well, how nice of you.

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:04.840
That sounds much more pleasant than 
being sucked into a black hole.

00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:05.970
You're right.

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:07.600
If that's a black hole...

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:09.990
Since its extremely high density and mass

00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:15.420
make its gravitational pull so powerful 
that it sucks in both objects and light...

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:16.510
Kotoko.

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:21.200
If a human is sucked into a black hole...

00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:23.040
Kotoko!

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:27.120
We don't need to test that right now.

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:28.770
Oh, sorry.

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:31.980
It looks like they're going 
to use that capturing device.

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:35.890
Since it's so important, I'll tell you again.

00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:42.990
Using this, I'll be able to quickly take your 
creativity back to space in perfect condition.

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:46.460
He seems determined to fight.

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:48.760
Wait, indeed.

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:58.010
I think we should stop stealing, indeed!

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:34.920
Misa-sama, what did you say?

00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:39.650
I said we should stop stealing, indeed.

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:40.730
What?

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:44.310
Oh, did my explanation sound too violent?

00:03:44.310 --> 00:03:48.400
We'll be bringing them 
back without hurting them.

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:49.480
Now then...

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:57.760
I don't want to steal them anymore, indeed!

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:03.840
Not steal them?

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:05.940
Not steal them?

00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:08.180
I'm so surprised, I repeated myself!

00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:10.960
Misa-sama?

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:13.390
What are you talking about?

00:04:14.070 --> 00:04:16.550
I understand now, indeed.

00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:18.360
Instead of stealing...

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:23.530
When you make things 
yourself, they shine more.

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:26.820
They're so wonderful.

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:31.830
And when they're stolen 
from you, your heart hurts.

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:36.460
So we shouldn't steal other people's 
things from them, indeed!

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:38.810
What are you talking about?

00:04:38.810 --> 00:04:43.100
Stealing is our identity as Scoopers.

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:46.040
Are you rejecting our very existence?

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:51.420
These objects—these products of 
civilization—are our lifeline.

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:55.030
Without these trophies, the Scoopers would

00:04:55.030 --> 00:05:00.980
simply wander through space, aimlessly 
and without creativity, until we die out!

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:04.800
These are all things you've stolen?

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:07.260
You aliens really are thieves.

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:09.530
This is too amazing. Too amazing!

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:12.430
I was so surprised, I repeated myself, too.

00:05:12.430 --> 00:05:15.740
Kotoko, do you want to 
become a Scooper again?

00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:18.420
No, thank you.

00:05:18.700 --> 00:05:22.630
I'm really glad I met you all, indeed.

00:05:23.540 --> 00:05:24.620
Misa-chan...

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:31.060
I was so bored all the time, indeed.

00:06:08.740 --> 00:06:11.220
Wow!

00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:13.680
Princess, be careful.

00:06:15.140 --> 00:06:19.360
I was always so excited when we 
first arrived on a new planet.

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:21.480
They all seemed so shiny, indeed.

00:06:22.450 --> 00:06:23.370
But...

00:06:24.120 --> 00:06:27.460
Princess, all of that belongs to us.

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:33.610
As usual, I shall deliver it to you.
Do look forward to it.

00:06:33.610 --> 00:06:35.370
Indeed!

00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:46.390
Princess, take a look at this first.

00:06:47.130 --> 00:06:48.970
What is it, indeed?

00:06:52.180 --> 00:06:53.150
I see.

00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:02.490
So, what happens now?

00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:06.250
Um, that's it.

00:07:06.250 --> 00:07:07.860
How boring, indeed.

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:09.990
How about this?

00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:12.780
Argh!

00:07:14.270 --> 00:07:15.800
And this?

00:07:20.910 --> 00:07:21.790
Uh...

00:07:22.600 --> 00:07:24.820
How disappointing, indeed...

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:32.690
How do you use that?

00:07:43.780 --> 00:07:45.400
Hmm...

00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:52.360
My excitement never lasted long, indeed.

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:03.810
According to my analysis,

00:08:03.810 --> 00:08:08.130
this is a device called an Amatsumara that 
causes the things you imagine to materialize.

00:08:08.130 --> 00:08:12.720
As Scoopers have no imagination, 
there's no way for us to use it.

00:08:17.630 --> 00:08:20.380
Princess, one moment, please.

00:08:28.520 --> 00:08:29.880
What do you think?

00:08:29.880 --> 00:08:32.880
I have imitated the creatures 
of our next planet.

00:08:33.940 --> 00:08:36.360
You look strange, indeed.

00:08:38.320 --> 00:08:39.590
In that case...

00:08:44.640 --> 00:08:46.320
How about this?

00:08:46.320 --> 00:08:47.650
That's cute, indeed!

00:08:47.650 --> 00:08:50.200
What kind of planet is it?

00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:55.840
Nagoya
Points of Interest

00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:54.200
The next planet is called Earth.

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:55.840
Earth?

00:08:55.840 --> 00:08:58.930
Earth has lots of wonderful culture.

00:08:59.840 --> 00:09:01.280
It's so shiny, indeed!

00:09:01.280 --> 00:09:02.300
It is.

00:09:02.300 --> 00:09:03.890
Don't you think it's wonderful?

00:09:04.300 --> 00:09:08.590
Shining golden monuments 
that are full of life.

00:09:08.590 --> 00:09:11.650
This is culture. This is culture!

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:14.610
It's so wonderful, I said it twice!

00:09:15.460 --> 00:09:18.020
I-Indeed...

00:09:26.930 --> 00:09:28.540
Indeed!

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:30.880
Do you like it?

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:33.710
I've never seen anything so wonderful, indeed!

00:09:33.710 --> 00:09:37.510
I must have it. I must have it, indeed!

00:09:37.510 --> 00:09:40.300
It's so wonderful, I said it twice, indeed.

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:44.020
I want to dress like these Earthlings, indeed.

00:09:49.670 --> 00:09:51.490
Impressive, Princess.

00:09:51.490 --> 00:09:55.360
Your imitation is just as good as mine.

00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:58.700
Now we can blend in with 
the Earthlings perfectly.

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:04.160
By the way, this planet uses something called 
"names" to differentiate between individuals.

00:10:04.780 --> 00:10:13.640
This beautiful object I have imitated 
is apparently called an "Ebifurya."

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:12.500
Fried Shrimp

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:12.500
An entire Ebifurya in a single bite!

00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:16.400
Fried Shrimp

00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:21.850
An entire Ebifurya in a single bite!

00:10:13.640 --> 00:10:16.560
What does this say?

00:10:16.560 --> 00:10:20.080
"Marunomisa," I believe.

00:10:20.080 --> 00:10:21.850
Marunomisa...

00:10:22.070 --> 00:10:24.260
Maruno Misa!

00:10:24.820 --> 00:10:28.730
I'm Maruno Misa, indeed!

00:10:33.070 --> 00:10:35.400
Wow, indeed!

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:40.380
Harajuku Station

00:10:36.260 --> 00:10:39.280
Apparently this area is called Harajuku.

00:10:39.280 --> 00:10:40.910
Harajuku...

00:11:05.020 --> 00:11:13.650
Such imaginative creatures may 
be able to use the Amatsumara.

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:26.810
What a noisy device.

00:11:27.230 --> 00:11:29.250
Misa-sama, are you all right?

00:11:29.250 --> 00:11:32.920
I love Harajuku, indeed!

00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:37.410
I want it all, indeed!

00:11:49.440 --> 00:11:51.560
Meow, meow.

00:11:54.600 --> 00:11:55.670
Good morning.

00:11:57.150 --> 00:11:58.530
Hey, what's the holdup?

00:12:15.860 --> 00:12:17.200
She's so cute!

00:12:17.200 --> 00:12:19.170
I won't deny that, but...

00:12:20.340 --> 00:12:27.640
The first time I met the three of you, 
I was really surprised, indeed.

00:12:28.930 --> 00:12:31.140
By the power you had

00:12:32.200 --> 00:12:33.870
to have fun creating

00:12:34.320 --> 00:12:36.980
wonderful things.

00:12:38.760 --> 00:12:45.910
Until I came to this planet, 
I had no idea what I wanted.

00:12:47.090 --> 00:12:48.870
But for the first time,

00:12:49.420 --> 00:12:51.660
I truly wanted

00:12:52.330 --> 00:12:59.500
to be like you, and create 
something wonderful.

00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:19.010
Then steal these people who are 
capable of creating wonderful things!

00:13:19.010 --> 00:13:20.290
Forever!

00:13:21.160 --> 00:13:23.740
I realized something, indeed.

00:13:23.740 --> 00:13:25.580
Realized what?

00:13:25.580 --> 00:13:28.440
That's not good enough.

00:13:28.440 --> 00:13:31.540
What I... What I really want is...

00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:32.940
What you really want is?

00:13:33.710 --> 00:13:37.670
To be wonderful. That's all, indeed.

00:13:39.620 --> 00:13:42.320
Like them.

00:13:42.320 --> 00:13:43.130
Huh?!

00:13:43.880 --> 00:13:45.000
Misa-chan...

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:49.850
I understand what it feels like 
to want to be like someone else.

00:13:49.850 --> 00:13:50.890
Huh?!

00:13:50.890 --> 00:13:52.430
I dont understand!

00:13:52.780 --> 00:13:56.240
Not what you're saying, 
and not Misa-sama's feelings, either!

00:13:56.240 --> 00:13:58.780
A Scooper should take what they want!

00:13:58.780 --> 00:14:01.250
Does your DNA not tell you to steal?

00:14:01.250 --> 00:14:03.070
No, it doesn't!

00:14:03.360 --> 00:14:04.930
Why don't you understand?

00:14:04.930 --> 00:14:08.300
Misa-chan's telling you that 
she's found her true self.

00:14:08.300 --> 00:14:09.970
She just wants to be wonderful.

00:14:09.970 --> 00:14:13.020
That feeling isn't something she can steal.

00:14:15.170 --> 00:14:17.010
I'm very familiar with that.

00:14:21.080 --> 00:14:24.550
And besides, DNA can't speak.

00:14:24.770 --> 00:14:29.830
DNA, also known as deoxyribonucleic 
acid, is a type of nucleic acid.

00:14:29.830 --> 00:14:33.080
As such, it exists only in macromolecular 
substances to transmit

00:14:33.080 --> 00:14:35.440
and express genetic information, and...

00:14:35.440 --> 00:14:36.180
Misa-chan.

00:14:40.240 --> 00:14:43.280
I wanted to be wonderful, too.

00:14:44.060 --> 00:14:48.780
I wanted to hold my head high and 
tell people that these were my drawings.

00:14:49.520 --> 00:14:53.240
That's what being wonderful meant to me.

00:14:53.620 --> 00:14:54.630
Rito...

00:14:54.630 --> 00:14:55.950
Rito-chan...

00:14:56.460 --> 00:14:58.220
After meeting Mari and Kotoko,

00:14:58.880 --> 00:15:00.350
I finally became wonderful.

00:15:02.250 --> 00:15:04.040
Limited Time

00:15:05.560 --> 00:15:10.130
This must be what it feels like to wait 
for your cue in a Broadway theater.

00:15:10.560 --> 00:15:13.850
Primadonna, it's curtain time.

00:15:14.320 --> 00:15:15.560
Don't rush me.

00:15:16.090 --> 00:15:18.640
The star always shows up late.

00:15:18.930 --> 00:15:21.000
I can't believe you're nervous, Mari.

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:22.980
You must be a rare diva.

00:15:23.640 --> 00:15:26.570
It's too bad this isn't Manhattan.

00:15:26.820 --> 00:15:30.660
But we're finally opening our own store.

00:15:30.660 --> 00:15:33.320
Of course I feel this way.

00:15:34.620 --> 00:15:38.040
What if people say our stuff isn't cute?

00:15:39.920 --> 00:15:43.630
We'll be seeing if the things 
we've made will be accepted

00:15:43.900 --> 00:15:48.340
in the great cultural center 
of Harajuku, after all.

00:15:52.840 --> 00:15:54.180
It'll be fine.

00:15:54.180 --> 00:15:57.000
We made them together.

00:15:57.000 --> 00:16:04.220
We'll bring in as many customers as 
Broadway to this backstreet in Harajuku.

00:16:04.220 --> 00:16:09.580
Mari-chan, shouldn't you be comparing 
us to the Champs-Élysées in Paris instead?

00:16:09.580 --> 00:16:11.840
It's a famous fashion street.

00:16:11.840 --> 00:16:13.920
To the east is Place de la Concorde,

00:16:13.920 --> 00:16:17.820
and to the west, three kilometers away, 
is the Arc de Triomphe.

00:16:17.820 --> 00:16:21.920
There's also Ladurée, where 
macarons were invented.

00:16:21.920 --> 00:16:22.870
Kotoko.

00:16:23.670 --> 00:16:26.880
That's enough about the Champs-Élysées.

00:16:26.880 --> 00:16:28.000
Oh, sorry.

00:16:30.790 --> 00:16:33.300
All right, it's time to open!

00:16:37.400 --> 00:16:39.720
Thank you!

00:16:39.720 --> 00:16:41.730
Come back soon!

00:16:48.510 --> 00:16:49.400
All right!

00:16:49.660 --> 00:16:50.640
Rito!

00:16:50.640 --> 00:16:53.820
The T-shirt I designed...

00:16:54.410 --> 00:16:55.410
We sold one!

00:16:57.060 --> 00:16:57.740
Yeah.

00:16:58.180 --> 00:16:59.580
That's great!

00:16:59.580 --> 00:17:00.580
Kotoko...

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:03.420
We sold one of our products!

00:17:03.420 --> 00:17:04.540
Yeah!

00:17:07.490 --> 00:17:10.340
Even we can make things.

00:17:10.340 --> 00:17:12.580
Let's keep making more.

00:17:12.580 --> 00:17:13.550
Yeah!

00:17:14.520 --> 00:17:17.760
<i>As long as I'm with Kotoko and Mari,</i>

00:17:18.560 --> 00:17:20.140
<i>I can do it.</i>

00:17:25.860 --> 00:17:27.360
<i>I can keep creating.</i>

00:17:31.230 --> 00:17:37.490
Mari and Kotoko are the ones who taught 
me that even I could be wonderful.

00:17:38.190 --> 00:17:42.700
Because we were together, 
we became wonderful in this city.

00:17:43.660 --> 00:17:48.450
You could probably be wonderful, 
too, if we created together.

00:17:49.970 --> 00:17:55.880
I think you understand the joy of creativity.

00:17:56.350 --> 00:18:01.850
So you can become the wonderful 
person you dream of being.

00:18:01.850 --> 00:18:04.680
Thank you, indeed.

00:18:05.100 --> 00:18:06.670
Me, too.

00:18:06.670 --> 00:18:09.330
I was always alone.

00:18:09.330 --> 00:18:11.520
No one ever paid attention to me.

00:18:12.020 --> 00:18:15.960
But then I met Rito-chan and 
Mari-chan in Harajuku.

00:18:16.600 --> 00:18:19.320
They acknowledged me.

00:18:19.320 --> 00:18:23.700
So I like to think I've become 
a little wonderful, too.

00:18:24.470 --> 00:18:26.230
You are wonderful, Kotoko.

00:18:26.230 --> 00:18:27.410
Mari-chan...

00:18:27.700 --> 00:18:34.220
I also wanted to be wonderful, 
like the people I admired.

00:18:35.160 --> 00:18:39.870
But in the end, I was just 
copying someone else.

00:18:41.560 --> 00:18:45.560
But I realized that with Rito and Kotoko,

00:18:46.160 --> 00:18:49.900
even I could create wonderful things.

00:18:49.900 --> 00:18:52.270
I could help them.

00:18:52.980 --> 00:18:58.990
I realized doing that instead of 
copying others would make me shine.

00:19:01.540 --> 00:19:06.840
You three really are wonderful, indeed.

00:19:07.540 --> 00:19:11.920
Even though there's no one 
left in this ruined city.

00:19:12.330 --> 00:19:13.260
Huh?

00:19:13.260 --> 00:19:14.860
No one?

00:19:14.860 --> 00:19:17.010
Ruined city?

00:19:17.010 --> 00:19:18.460
Yes, indeed.

00:19:18.460 --> 00:19:24.040
You've been imagining all the 
people and buildings, indeed!

00:19:24.040 --> 00:19:25.500
Imagining?

00:19:25.500 --> 00:19:27.700
The people and the buildings?

00:19:27.700 --> 00:19:28.470
What do you mean?

00:19:28.470 --> 00:19:31.270
Misa-sama, don't say another word!

00:19:32.560 --> 00:19:36.610
When you wished to protect the city...

00:19:37.460 --> 00:19:39.780
<i>I want to protect the city.</i>

00:19:40.260 --> 00:19:41.880
<i>I want to stay here.</i>

00:19:42.400 --> 00:19:44.280
<i>This place is everything to me.</i>

00:19:44.830 --> 00:19:47.820
Your imaginations...

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:11.540
recreated Harajuku and the people in it.

00:20:11.540 --> 00:20:12.770
That can't be.

00:20:13.110 --> 00:20:14.130
No way.

00:20:14.130 --> 00:20:16.440
E-Even if we did,

00:20:16.440 --> 00:20:19.980
wouldn't destroying the Amatsumara make 
the people and buildings disappear?

00:20:20.330 --> 00:20:25.840
The Amatsumara isn't the only thing 
that makes your thoughts materialize!

00:20:25.840 --> 00:20:29.990
That parfait that absorbed 
the power of the Amatsumara

00:20:29.990 --> 00:20:33.210
also has the power to create, indeed.

00:20:33.800 --> 00:20:35.320
W-Wait a minute.

00:20:35.320 --> 00:20:37.960
We made all the people, too?

00:20:38.290 --> 00:20:41.330
That's right. It's amazing, indeed.

00:20:41.330 --> 00:20:43.720
You can create people just by imagining them.

00:20:44.580 --> 00:20:49.060
Then the people who praised my drawings...

00:20:52.340 --> 00:20:53.850
Yes, indeed.

00:20:53.850 --> 00:20:56.940
Your imagination created them, indeed.

00:20:57.330 --> 00:20:59.230
And our customers at Park...

00:20:59.620 --> 00:21:01.070
Of course, indeed.

00:21:01.280 --> 00:21:03.050
Huh? What?

00:21:03.580 --> 00:21:05.460
Wait a minute.

00:21:05.460 --> 00:21:07.680
You can't mean...

00:21:07.680 --> 00:21:09.740
And Sayumin?

00:21:09.740 --> 00:21:11.370
Yes, indeed.

00:21:11.560 --> 00:21:16.330
Your imaginations are 
truly powerful, indeed.

00:21:16.830 --> 00:21:19.880
You made Sayumin-san out of nothing...

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:22.840
and killed her yourselves.

00:21:23.540 --> 00:21:27.380
Sayumin never existed at all?

00:21:27.940 --> 00:21:34.980
In other words, we've been inside 
a fantasy this whole time?

00:21:34.980 --> 00:21:37.810
That's what you're saying, 
right, Misa-chan?

00:21:39.300 --> 00:21:40.890
Fantasy?

00:21:43.020 --> 00:21:46.540
It's all a fantasy, indeed!

00:23:25.490 --> 00:23:27.500
Ebifurya, I'm sorry, indeed.

00:23:27.500 --> 00:23:29.130
I've been hiding something from you.

00:23:29.130 --> 00:23:31.030
Misa-sama, what is it?

00:23:31.030 --> 00:23:32.280
The truth is, you're...

00:23:32.280 --> 00:23:34.180
I'm so curious. Please tell me.

00:23:34.180 --> 00:23:37.440
You're not a fried shrimp. 
